  "notes": "WEB DNG numbers Greek Daniel as 14 chapters. Prayer of Azariah and Song of the Three = 3:24-3:90 (67 Greek-only verses inserted between Hebrew 3:23 and 3:24; WEB 3:91-97 = Hebrew 3:24-30). Within it: narrative 3:24-25, Azariah's prayer 3:26-45, narrative 3:46-51, Song of the Three Young Men 3:52-90. Susanna = ch.13 (13:1-64), Bel and the Dragon = ch.14 (14:1-42). WEB follows the Theodotion form with Susanna as ch.13 after Daniel 12. People in 1:1-3:23 and 3:91-12:13 are Hebrew-parallel and intentionally not recorded. Unnamed group members (Susanna's two maids and children, the servants, the 70 priests of Bel and their families, the Babylonian conspirators) are not recorded as individuals. Doubtful: Daniel of Susanna = canonical Daniel (traditional); Habakkuk = canonical prophet (anachronism under Cyrus); Cyrus refs include the 'the king' verses of ch.14."
